.SH DESCRIPTION
.B \%waddstr
writes the characters of the (null-terminated) string
.I str
to the window
.IR win ,
as if by calling \fB\%waddch\fP(3X) for each
.I char
in
.IR str .
.B \%waddnstr
is similar,
but writes at most
.I n
characters.
If
.I n
is \-1,
.B \%waddnstr
writes the entire string.
\fB\%ncurses\fP(3X) describes the variants of these functions.
